# Agent Git Baseline

This is the intent layer only. It is advisory — an agent can ignore it, and
nothing here is copied or enforced by a plain `git clone`. Real enforcement is
server-side (branch rulesets, required status checks, push protection, signed
commits) — see this repo's README.

## Rules

1. Never assume a local pre-commit hook will catch anything. Hooks live in
   `.git/hooks`, are not copied by clone, and are not run by API-driven agent
   pushes.
2. Small, single-concern commits — one intent per commit.
3. State blast radius in the commit message or PR description for anything
   touching shared, security-relevant, or trust-boundary code.
4. Do not self-approve. If this agent opened the PR, it does not also approve
   it, merge without required review, or bypass a required status check.
5. A "Verified" badge on a commit is not proof of human review — server-created
   commits can carry it too. Don't cite the badge as review evidence.
6. Flag anything shaped like a hallucinated bulk change (many PRs in a short
   window, especially touching credentials/config/CI) and confirm with the
   user before pushing.

## Why this needs a server-side layer too

Client-side controls (local hooks) are bypassed entirely by API-driven agents —
they don't run a local git process, and cloning never copies `.git/hooks`. An
agent hallucinating from a malformed prompt can open dozens of PRs overnight
with plaintext credentials, sailing past a secret scanner that only runs as a
pre-commit hook. This rule file is step 1 of 3 (intent → enforcement →
attribution) — see the README for the other two.
